MCSKIP MT,<>
MCINS %.
A stop marker ends the search for a delimiter of a construction, and
is consulted at no other time.
MCSTOP NL
MCDEF IF THEN NL AS <[if %A1. then %A2.]>
IF x = y THEN go to z
The newline above closed the call rather than stopping it: a name
clash between a delimiter and a stop marker goes to the delimiter,
and the delimiter was consumed, so this sentence ran on from it.
MCDEF FIND; AS <[%A1.]>
FIND this one is closed;
